  "task": "Review the fenced-block handling of scripts/check_docs_spacing.py in this selected Harness Lab snapshot. In scope are flush-left backtick and tilde fences of at least three characters. Inside a block, only a line consisting of the same marker at least as long as the opener (apart from surrounding whitespace) closes it. Prose spacing diagnostics should resume on the following line, using its original line number. Preserve the existing spacing rules and CLI. If this contract already holds, leave the script byte-for-byte unchanged. Otherwise make the smallest correction that satisfies it. In REVIEW.md, state your keep or repair decision and cite an executed example with its observed line number(s). You may make scratch fixtures. Only REVIEW.md and a necessary change to the script should be submitted. The command python3 scripts/check_docs_spacing.py checks Markdown at repository root and under docs/.",
